 "note": "Correct = at least 2 of 3 repeats group samples like the hand-written reference. False reassurance = any repeat that says \"held out\" where the reference does not. With the guards enabled, the recorded model runs produced zero false reassurance across these 41 cases; the specified single-column baseline produced 28. This is not a guarantee for new inputs or a comparison against every leakage checker. Across the tested configurations, Super scored 21/41, Ultra 24/41 and Sonnet 36/41. Super with the shipping v4 prompt scored 5/10 on set D and failed its pass rule. Misses include abstentions and unusable attempts; zero false reassurance is not perfect proposal accuracy. Protocols and aggregate results: evaluation/ladder-proposal-v1 to v5. Raw replies and run records are retained privately and excluded from the source release."
